  "body": "The post-merge run 43977363817 (batch tier) on `fac6c8e8d22cb39bb0a4c18644b4ec1c4dbd2db6` failed 18 tests in six `camcraft-app` suites. The previous run (43970156626, after batch 15) failed at compile. Thus the cause can be in batch 15 or in batch 16.\n\nFailing tests:\n\n- `pocket3d_open_side`:\n  - `multiaxis_rough_post_refuses_a_part_added_after_clean_generation_on_rotated_stock`\n  - `pocket3d_post_refuses_a_part_added_after_clean_generation_on_rotated_stock`\n- `circular_pick_law`:\n  - `a_picked_circle_cut_below_its_floor_gouges_and_never_posts_where_the_sim_cannot_judge`\n- `kept_parts_live`:\n  - `a_part_added_into_a_stock_source_cut_on_a_turned_stock_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `a_fixture_untagged_then_moved_into_a_part_source_cut_on_a_turned_stock_is_refused_by_name`\n  - `a_neighbour_moved_into_a_part_source_cut_on_a_turned_stock_is_refused_by_name`\n- `stock_source_holes`:\n  - `a_hole_kind_off_the_stock_into_the_part_gouges_and_never_posts`\n  - `stock_source_chamfer_refusal_names_cause_and_part_as_source_workaround`\n  - `a_part_added_under_a_stock_source_drill_is_judged_at_the_post_by_the_hole_law`\n- `trochoid_law`:\n  - `a_whole_model_trochoid_under_the_floor_gouges_and_never_posts_where_the_sim_cannot_judge`\n  - `a_whole_model_trochoid_through_the_pocket_wall_gouges_and_never_posts`\n  - `a_picked_trochoid_that_fits_its_floor_but_sinks_under_it_never_posts`\n- `keep_law` (each in `::pocket_turned` and `::adaptive_turned`):\n  - `a_whole_model_area_offset_into_the_part_gouges_and_never_posts`\n  - `a_whole_model_extension_into_the_part_gouges_and_never_posts`\n  - `stock_source::a_stock_source_area_offset_into_the_part_gouges_and_never_posts`\n\nMany tests use turned or rotated stock. The gate log does not show the panic text. The key question is open: does a program that must be refused now post, or does the refusal only arrive with a different text, name or stage? The claimant adds the answer after a local reproduction.\n\nMain is red in wrong-output suites. Thus this issue is `P1`.\n",
